From c1e6ce3fa3f165c9efca6f12ba542be89e61c347 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 20:24:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/31] a210: build: fix defconfig drops and more 6.6->7.0 API
 drift

Second batch of v7.0 build fixes.

defconfig (arch/riscv/configs/a210_evb_defconfig): the vendor 6.6
savedefconfig relied on symbols that 7.0 no longer auto-enables, which
silently dropped whole subsystems at olddefconfig. Restore them:
- CONFIG_ETHTOOL_NETLINK=y: STMMAC_ETH now depends on it; without it the
  entire stmmac stack (and DWMAC_ZHIHE ethernet) was dropped. STMMAC_ETH
  in turn selects RESET_CONTROLLER, which brings back RESET_A210.
- CONFIG_GPIOLIB=y: was off, dropping every GPIO driver (GPIO_DWAPB,
  GPIO_PCA953X, GPIO_SYSFS).
- CONFIG_I2C_DESIGNWARE_CORE=y: I2C_DESIGNWARE_PLATFORM is now gated
  behind it; without it the DesignWare i2c controller dropped.
Also drop four non-essential drivers from the defconfig that carry
heavier API drift and are not needed for boot/install/network; they are
left to port in a later pass: RISCV_XUANTIE_TH1520_CPUFREQ,
RISCV_ZHIHE_CPUFREQ, RPMSG_TH1520, A210_BMU, SPI_DW_QUAD.

Source fixes:
- pwm-thead: port to the new pwm_chip model (devm_pwmchip_alloc +
  pwmchip_get_drvdata, pwmchip_parent() for the parent device).
- Add includes pruned from 7.0's transitive headers: <linux/platform_device.h>
  (th1520-mailbox, zhihe-mailbox, th1520-ddr-pmu), <linux/vmalloc.h>
  (th1520_aon_pd, a210-pd), <linux/of.h>+<linux/platform_device.h>
  (reset-a210).
- dwmac-zhihe: fix_mac_speed() takes int speed; drop the removed
  stmmac_remove_config_dt() (devm config_dt auto-frees); .remove_new ->
  .remove.
- th1520_aon_pd: genpd xlate callback takes const struct of_phandle_args *.
- {th1520,zhihe}_proc_debug: ALT_CMO_OP ops are upper-case now
  (FLUSH/CLEAN/INVAL); CBO_flush/CBO_clean no longer exist.

Co-developed-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lance Albertson <lance@osuosl.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
